# Code owners for arqtiqa/arqtos-sdk-go
#
# @mw-io is the REVIEWING identity for arqtiqa repositories; @mw-aqa is the
# authoring identity. The split is deliberate: GitHub does not let a pull
# request author approve their own PR, so a repository whose only owner is also
# its only author has an unsatisfiable review requirement and every merge
# becomes an admin bypass. Two identities make the review rule real instead of
# ceremonial.
#
# Keep this file in step with the branch-protection setting
# `require_code_owner_reviews` — a protection rule that points at a CODEOWNERS
# file which does not exist reads stricter than it enforces.

